{"card": {"id": "quantum_hamming_15_7_3", "kind": "family", "identity": {"canonical_name": "Quantum Hamming code", "variant": "fifteen-qubit CSS block", "aliases": ["15-qubit quantum Hamming code", "15-qubit CSS Hamming block"]}, "presentation": {"orienting_view": {"status": "available", "kind": "stabilizer-incidence"}, "guided_tour": {"status": "available"}}, "eczoo": {"status": "mapped", "zoo_id": "stab_15_7_3", "classification": "exact-family", "source": {"repository_url": "https://github.com/errorcorrectionzoo/eczoo_data", "commit": "b2437d9e2dc09284e04c66ef72ee81b7ed7bd129", "retrieved_on": "2026-08-05", "path": "codes/quantum/qubits/small_distance/small/15/stab_15_7_3.yml", "sha256": "4374e65a031268e497974fce1c6b083fc581f0a64f418ca733f28864d9f61315", "page_url": "https://errorcorrectionzoo.org/c/stab_15_7_3", "blob_url": "https://github.com/errorcorrectionzoo/eczoo_data/blob/b2437d9e2dc09284e04c66ef72ee81b7ed7bd129/codes/quantum/qubits/small_distance/small/15/stab_15_7_3.yml"}}, "description": "A fixed CSS block whose qubits are labeled by the fifteen nonzero vectors of F_2^4. The four coordinate bits form a classical Hamming parity-check matrix, and using that same matrix for both X and Z checks gives eight commuting stabilizers. The code encodes seven qubits and corrects any one physical-qubit Pauli error. It is not the [[15,1,3]] quantum Reed\u2013Muller code: that block is obtained only after six additional independent Z constraints fix six of these logical degrees of freedom.", "views": [{"rung": "R1", "type": "symplectic-css-checks", "description": "Duplicating the four binary Hamming rows into X and Z sectors gives eight commuting symplectic generators. This executable matrix fixes qubit and syndrome ordering for rank, centralizer, and exact-distance calculations.", "origin": {"kind": "derived", "converter": "quantum_hamming_15_7_3.build -> CheckMatrix.from_css", "version": "v1"}, "refs": ["steane1996simple", "calderbank1996good"]}, {"rung": "R2", "type": "hamming-column-css", "description": "Order the columns as 0001, 0010, ..., 1111. Every nonzero four-bit syndrome is therefore the address of exactly one physical qubit. The four coordinate rows are mutually orthogonal over F_2, so duplicating them as X and Z checks produces a commuting CSS presentation.", "origin": {"kind": "canonical"}, "refs": ["steane1996simple", "calderbank1996good"]}, {"rung": "R5", "type": "syndrome-address", "description": "A single X error anticommutes with the Z checks in the column named by its location, and a single Z error gives the same address in the X syndrome. A Y error activates both sectors. Thus the classical Hamming lookup rule survives intact, once for each Pauli component.", "origin": {"kind": "derived", "converter": "constructor.HAMMING_CHECKS column lookup", "version": "v1"}, "refs": ["gottesman1997stabilizer"]}, {"rung": "R1", "type": "stabilizer-containment", "description": "The [[15,7,3]] stabilizer is a strict subgroup of the repository's [[15,1,3]] quantum Reed\u2013Muller stabilizer in the shared nonzero-vector qubit order. Their four X checks agree. The Hamming Z row space sits inside the Reed\u2013Muller Z row space, whose six additional independent rows fix six Hamming logical Z values and leave one protected qubit.", "origin": {"kind": "derived", "converter": "constructor.reed_muller_gauge_out_witness + qeclib.gf2.rank", "version": "v1"}, "refs": ["steane1996simple", "steane1996quantumrm"]}, {"rung": "R5", "type": "finite-geometry-automorphisms", "description": "GL(4,2) acts on the fifteen nonzero column labels. Each invertible linear relabeling preserves the Hamming row space, hence gives a physical coordinate permutation that preserves the stabilizer. Its logical action must still be reduced in the fourteen-dimensional logical symplectic quotient; it is not merely a relabeling of seven named logical qubits.", "origin": {"kind": "curated", "ref": "grassl2013automorphisms"}, "refs": ["grassl2013automorphisms"]}, {"rung": "R5", "type": "hamming-bound-audit", "description": "The word \u201cHamming\u201d refers to the inherited classical parity-check construction, not saturation of the nondegenerate quantum Hamming bound. The constructor-derived n, k, and distance leave unused syndrome space after all single-qubit Pauli errors are counted.", "origin": {"kind": "derived", "converter": "instance claims + single-error sphere count", "version": "v1"}, "refs": ["gottesman1997stabilizer"]}], "categories": [{"id": "small-code", "origin": {"kind": "curated", "ref": "steane1996simple"}}, {"id": "css", "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}], "refs": ["calderbank1996good", "steane1996simple", "gottesman1997stabilizer", "grassl2013automorphisms", "steane1996quantumrm"], "params": {}, "visual_instance": "n15", "tier": "T2", "fit": {"platforms": ["hardware-agnostic-fixed-block", "all-to-all-connected-register"], "tasks": ["exact-small-block-decoding", "concatenated-quantum-memory", "logical-automorphism-study"]}, "decoders": [{"id": "lookup-table", "status": "standard", "noise": "one fixed block under a single physical-qubit Pauli error with perfect X- and Z-stabilizer syndromes", "notes": "Read each nonzero four-bit syndrome as one of the fifteen Hamming columns. The Z-check syndrome locates an X component, the X-check syndrome locates a Z component, and simultaneous addresses identify a Y error. This exact finite rule is not a threshold claim; noisy extraction and concatenation require a circuit- or hierarchy-specific decoder.", "refs": ["gottesman1997stabilizer", "steane1996simple"]}], "realizations": [], "relations": [{"type": "special_case_of", "target": "quantum_hamming_css", "how": "This fixed block is the four-coordinate member of the binary CSS quantum Hamming construction. The relation records that family specialization without replacing this EC-Zoo-mapped fixed-block identity by the variable-length family.", "refs": ["steane1996simple", "calderbank1996good"]}, {"type": "gauge_fixes_to", "target": "quantum_reed_muller_15", "how": "In the shared ordering of the fifteen nonzero four-bit labels, retain the four Hamming X checks and enlarge the four-dimensional Hamming Z row space to the ten-dimensional orthogonal complement of the coordinate rows plus the all-one row. The six added commuting Z constraints fix six Hamming logical degrees of freedom, changing k from seven to one. The entry regression verifies both row-space containment and the target constructor, so the two blocks are related by gauge-out rather than identified as alternative presentations.", "refs": ["steane1996simple", "steane1996quantumrm"]}], "operations": [{"gate": "CNOT between aligned blocks", "mechanism": "transversal", "level": "Clifford", "cost": "one layer of fifteen pairwise physical CNOTs; the pairing of the seven logical control-target pairs depends on the declared logical basis, and routing plus syndrome extraction are additional", "origin": {"kind": "claimed", "ref": "gottesman1997stabilizer"}}, {"gate": "logical Clifford transformations induced by GL(4,2)", "mechanism": "transversal", "level": "Clifford", "cost": "one physical permutation of the fifteen nonzero-vector coordinates; hardware routing is additional and the induced seven-qubit symplectic action must be tracked in a chosen logical basis", "origin": {"kind": "claimed", "ref": "grassl2013automorphisms"}}, {"gate": "gauge-out to the [[15,1,3]] quantum Reed\u2013Muller block", "mechanism": "gauge-fixing", "level": "code conversion with logical-dimension reduction", "cost": "measure six independent Z-type normalizer constraints and condition the Pauli frame on their outcomes; only the selected remaining logical qubit is preserved", "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}]}, "instances": [{"label": "n15", "params": {}, "claims": [{"property": "n", "value": 15, "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}, {"property": "k", "value": 7, "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}, {"property": "d", "exact": 3, "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}, {"property": "css", "value": true, "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}]}], "tier": "T2", "lattice": null, "schedule": null, "scene": {"schema": "qec-atlas-scene-v2", "dimension": 2, "origin": {"kind": "verified", "method": "quantum-hamming-15-nonzero-column-incidence-v1"}, "coordinateSystem": {"kind": "cartesian", "origin": [0.0, 0.0]}, "camera": {"fit": "contain", "padding": 0.1, "minZoom": 0.5, "maxZoom": 8.0}, "layers": [{"id": "data", "label": "Data qubits", "kind": "data", "defaultVisible": true}, {"id": "incidence", "label": "Stabilizer incidence", "kind": "checks", "defaultVisible": true}], "nodes": [{"id": "q0", "position": [0.0, -1.0], "role": "data", "label": "q0 \u00b7 0001"}, {"id": "q1", "position": [0.406736643076, -0.913545457643], "role": "data", "label": "q1 \u00b7 0010"}, {"id": "q2", "position": [0.743144825477, -0.669130606359], "role": "data", "label": "q2 \u00b7 0011"}, {"id": "q3", "position": [0.951056516295, -0.309016994375], "role": "data", "label": "q3 \u00b7 0100"}, {"id": "q4", "position": [0.994521895368, 0.104528463268], "role": "data", "label": "q4 \u00b7 0101"}, {"id": "q5", "position": [0.866025403784, 0.5], "role": "data", "label": "q5 \u00b7 0110"}, {"id": "q6", "position": [0.587785252292, 0.809016994375], "role": "data", "label": "q6 \u00b7 0111"}, {"id": "q7", "position": [0.207911690818, 0.978147600734], "role": "data", "label": "q7 \u00b7 1000"}, {"id": "q8", "position": [-0.207911690818, 0.978147600734], "role": "data", "label": "q8 \u00b7 1001"}, {"id": "q9", "position": [-0.587785252292, 0.809016994375], "role": "data", "label": "q9 \u00b7 1010"}, {"id": "q10", "position": [-0.866025403784, 0.5], "role": "data", "label": "q10 \u00b7 1011"}, {"id": "q11", "position": [-0.994521895368, 0.104528463268], "role": "data", "label": "q11 \u00b7 1100"}, {"id": "q12", "position": [-0.951056516295, -0.309016994375], "role": "data", "label": "q12 \u00b7 1101"}, {"id": "q13", "position": [-0.743144825477, -0.669130606359], "role": "data", "lab